                             REQUIRED REFERENCES
##############################################################################

 Description of the relativistic four-component DFT method for calculation
 of the electronic g-tensor is presented for the first time in Ref [1]
 and is further validated in Ref [2].

 [1] M. Repisky, S. Komorovsky, E. Malkin, O.L. Malkina,
     and V.G. Malkin, Chem. Phys. Lett. 488, 94-97 (2010).
     [DOI: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cplett.2010.01.077]

 [2] P. J. Cherry, S. Komorovsky, V. G. Malkin,
     and O. L. Malkina, Mol. Phys. 115, 75-89 (2017).
     [DOI: https://doi.org/10.1080/00268976.2016.1191688]

 XCFun: a library of DFT exchange-correlation functionals

 [3] U. Ekström, et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. 6, 1971-1980 (2010)
     [DOI: https://doi.org/10.1021/ct100117s]


